WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.101 --> 00:00:07.638
So I vividly remember
my first anxiety attack.

00:00:09.073 --> 00:00:10.775
It's kind of like I feel right now.

00:00:10.808 --> 00:00:12.143
(Laughter)

00:00:12.143 --> 00:00:13.744
Whoo, is it hot in here?

00:00:13.744 --> 00:00:15.446
(Laughter)

00:00:15.479 --> 00:00:16.680
It's hot in here.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:17.748
(Laughter)

00:00:17.748 --> 00:00:24.121
This wave of fear crashed over me,
and my heart started to pound.

00:00:24.155 --> 00:00:27.324
My breathing got ahead of me
and out of control.

00:00:27.324 --> 00:00:29.193
My face felt hot.

00:00:29.193 --> 00:00:30.394
It's hot in here, right?

00:00:30.394 --> 00:00:31.395
(Laughter)

00:00:31.429 --> 00:00:32.596
Yeah, it's hot.

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:36.367
And I got doused in this really
uncomfortable cold sweat.

00:00:38.636 --> 00:00:40.304
It was a life-changing moment,

00:00:40.337 --> 00:00:44.742
because I made a decision,
right there and then,

00:00:44.775 --> 00:00:50.681
to dedicate my career to ridding our world
of this feeling, anxiety.

00:00:52.583 --> 00:00:55.319
So that was more than two decades ago.

00:00:57.154 --> 00:00:58.322
Work in progress.

00:00:58.355 --> 00:01:01.025
(Laughter)

00:01:01.058 --> 00:01:02.760
I became a clinical psychologist.

00:01:02.793 --> 00:01:04.929
I became a professor.

00:01:04.962 --> 00:01:07.498
I started an anxiety treatment center.

00:01:08.399 --> 00:01:10.901
And then, I realized,
at some point along the way,

00:01:10.901 --> 00:01:15.806
that eradicating anxiety
from our lives would not be beneficial.

00:01:20.478 --> 00:01:23.414
Sometimes, anxiety interferes
with your life.

00:01:23.447 --> 00:01:25.483
That's clinical anxiety.

00:01:25.516 --> 00:01:28.853
And yes, you do want
to get rid of that clinical anxiety,

00:01:28.886 --> 00:01:30.988
with the help of a professional.

00:01:31.021 --> 00:01:33.557
But other times, many times ...

00:01:35.159 --> 00:01:38.295
it's uncomfortable, it's uncontrollable.

00:01:38.329 --> 00:01:39.897
Did I mention it's hot in here?

00:01:39.897 --> 00:01:41.365
(Laughter)

00:01:42.166 --> 00:01:43.334
It's intense.

00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:44.869
But that's a good thing.

00:01:44.902 --> 00:01:46.337
It's a good thing.

00:01:50.908 --> 00:01:55.312
Many of the greatest leaders
in human history,

00:01:55.346 --> 00:01:57.915
certainly in recent history,

00:01:57.948 --> 00:02:02.086
they were forged in a cauldron of anxiety.

00:02:03.854 --> 00:02:06.790
Once, early in his career,
Sir Winston Churchill,

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:10.594
he froze for three full minutes
in the House of Commons,

00:02:10.628 --> 00:02:11.896
giving a speech.

00:02:14.365 --> 00:02:16.500
He fought against his phobia,

00:02:16.534 --> 00:02:17.902
faced his fears head-on,

00:02:17.935 --> 00:02:21.438
and he went on to become
one of the greatest orators

00:02:21.472 --> 00:02:23.073
of the 20th century.

00:02:24.642 --> 00:02:26.143
In the 1990s,

00:02:26.177 --> 00:02:30.447
after a box-office flop, Oprah Winfrey,

00:02:30.481 --> 00:02:33.884
she turned to food
to drown out her feelings,

00:02:33.918 --> 00:02:35.386
to suppress her emotions.

00:02:35.419 --> 00:02:39.056
She ended up feeling
emotionally numb for six weeks,

00:02:39.089 --> 00:02:41.392
and during that period of great anxiety,

00:02:41.425 --> 00:02:47.731
she learned the importance of letting go
of her expectations for success.

00:02:47.765 --> 00:02:49.667
She went on to become a media icon.

00:02:50.634 --> 00:02:52.236
And speaking of icons ...

00:02:53.904 --> 00:02:59.410
The first time Taylor Swift sang
the national anthem at a football game,

00:02:59.443 --> 00:03:01.645
she felt paralyzed with fear.

00:03:03.914 --> 00:03:06.584
What she learned is to share
her feelings with others.

00:03:07.418 --> 00:03:08.552
Listen to her lyrics.

00:03:08.586 --> 00:03:10.788
Many of them speak about her own anxiety.

00:03:10.821 --> 00:03:13.591
And now, well, apparently,
she can “shake it off.”

00:03:13.624 --> 00:03:17.628
(Laughter)

00:03:17.661 --> 00:03:20.197
Anxiety is an emotion,

00:03:20.231 --> 00:03:22.132
like any other emotion,

00:03:22.166 --> 00:03:25.135
and it can do so much good for you.

00:03:25.169 --> 00:03:27.304
It can increase your resilience.

00:03:27.338 --> 00:03:29.440
It can strengthen your relationships.

00:03:30.241 --> 00:03:32.443
And it can help you to let go.

00:03:32.443 --> 00:03:34.245
When I first met Nicole ...

00:03:35.446 --> 00:03:38.582
she had hypochondriasis,
which is clinical health anxiety.

00:03:39.416 --> 00:03:41.885
Despite numerous MRIs to the contrary,

00:03:41.919 --> 00:03:44.855
she was convinced
that she had an aneurysm.

00:03:46.023 --> 00:03:50.060
Nicole's biggest fear
was that her anxiety would spike,

00:03:50.094 --> 00:03:53.364
her brain would explode,

00:03:53.397 --> 00:03:54.632
and she would drop dead,

00:03:54.665 --> 00:03:56.467
which would not be good.

00:03:56.467 --> 00:03:59.103
Nicole started to withdraw
from daily activities,

00:03:59.136 --> 00:04:02.973
and she recognized, rightfully,
that she needed professional help,

00:04:03.007 --> 00:04:04.308
so she came in.

00:04:05.476 --> 00:04:10.114
Nicole overcame her obsessions
with exposure therapy.

00:04:10.914 --> 00:04:12.316
She faced her fears.

00:04:12.349 --> 00:04:16.053
She embraced them head-on
in order to build resilience.

00:04:17.087 --> 00:04:18.689
She read stories about aneurysms.

00:04:18.722 --> 00:04:20.524
She watched videos about aneurysms.

00:04:20.557 --> 00:04:23.093
She went to a local neurology ward.

00:04:23.127 --> 00:04:27.197
Nicole overcame her obsessions,

00:04:27.197 --> 00:04:28.766
and she graduated from therapy.

00:04:28.766 --> 00:04:31.669
I was so happy and so proud of her.

00:04:32.436 --> 00:04:37.007
And then, a couple years later,
the phone rang.

00:04:37.007 --> 00:04:40.944
Nicole tells me she's pregnant
with a baby boy,

00:04:40.978 --> 00:04:45.382
but the doctors told her
that he would probably die

00:04:45.416 --> 00:04:48.886
because an ultrasound revealed
that he had an aneurysm.

00:04:48.919 --> 00:04:53.023
Now given Nicole's history,
I thought she would fall apart.

00:04:53.057 --> 00:04:56.126
But she didn't. She didn't.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:59.263
The baby needed life-saving surgery
shortly after birth,

00:04:59.296 --> 00:05:02.599
and Nicole, understandably
and very appropriately,

00:05:02.633 --> 00:05:07.137
was very anxious during the surgery,
as the doctors operated.

00:05:07.137 --> 00:05:09.039
But she stuck with it,

00:05:09.073 --> 00:05:10.474
and so did he.

00:05:11.175 --> 00:05:13.744
Today, he is a healthy,
thriving little boy,

00:05:13.777 --> 00:05:15.579
and also really cute, by the way.

00:05:15.612 --> 00:05:17.481
Really cute. Cute kid.

00:05:17.514 --> 00:05:22.786
And Nicole, she is a super-resilient mom
because she faced anxiety.

00:05:25.556 --> 00:05:28.225
You are a lot more like Nicole
than you think.

00:05:29.693 --> 00:05:33.297
There have been many times in your life
where you, too, embraced anxiety.

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:35.032
When you embraced the discomfort,

00:05:35.065 --> 00:05:39.370
when you persevered,
although you felt panicky and worried.

00:05:41.271 --> 00:05:43.574
And you've done this because,
deep in your heart,

00:05:43.607 --> 00:05:46.477
you know that you cannot
get rid of all of your anxiety,

00:05:46.477 --> 00:05:48.312
and it will always be uncomfortable.

00:05:48.345 --> 00:05:52.916
And that's why pushing against it
creates mental muscle tone,

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:54.151
which you need ...

00:05:55.652 --> 00:05:58.722
to crest over life's hurdles with grace.

00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:04.328
It can be difficult to love someone
who has anxiety,

00:06:04.361 --> 00:06:08.132
and it's probably even more
difficult to receive it.

00:06:09.032 --> 00:06:12.403
But deep human connection,

00:06:12.436 --> 00:06:15.072
deep emotional connections between people,

00:06:15.105 --> 00:06:17.474
requires vulnerability.

00:06:18.075 --> 00:06:22.079
So anxiety can be used to create intimacy.

00:06:24.014 --> 00:06:25.149
Think about it.

00:06:25.182 --> 00:06:28.652
In your own life, who are the people
who you feel closest to?

00:06:30.187 --> 00:06:32.623
Usually, it's those
who you've opened up to

00:06:32.656 --> 00:06:34.691
about your anxiety in some way.

00:06:35.926 --> 00:06:37.661
I myself --

00:06:37.694 --> 00:06:39.630
This is going to be hard, but I'll try.

00:06:42.566 --> 00:06:44.268
I'm terrified of failure.

00:06:44.968 --> 00:06:46.970
I'm terrified of professional failure.

00:06:47.805 --> 00:06:50.040
And I struggle with vulnerability.

00:06:50.841 --> 00:06:52.910
In some ways, this propelled me

00:06:52.943 --> 00:06:56.880
and fueled my drive
for professional success.

00:06:56.914 --> 00:07:00.651
But it created distance
in my relationships.

00:07:00.684 --> 00:07:03.787
When I first met my wonderful,
wonderful wife, Miri ...

00:07:05.355 --> 00:07:06.557
I put up a wall,

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:08.926
and I didn't speak enough
about my feelings,

00:07:08.959 --> 00:07:11.662
and I submerged my anxiety
by focusing on my work.

00:07:11.695 --> 00:07:13.664
Right? Pretty classic, right?

00:07:13.697 --> 00:07:14.698
(Laughter)

00:07:14.731 --> 00:07:17.701
You don't need to be a psychotherapist
to figure that one out.

00:07:17.734 --> 00:07:18.869
(Laughter)

00:07:20.137 --> 00:07:22.773
Of course, the feelings didn't go away.

00:07:22.806 --> 00:07:28.045
We all have this, like, chef,
in the back of our emotional kitchen.

00:07:28.078 --> 00:07:32.182
Well, my chef cooked up
these entrées of edginess,

00:07:32.216 --> 00:07:34.785
side orders of criticism

00:07:34.818 --> 00:07:36.520
and a whole bunch of other dishes

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:38.755
that I'm not going
to speak about in public.

00:07:38.755 --> 00:07:41.058
(Laughter)

00:07:41.391 --> 00:07:44.127
But Miri, thankfully, stuck with me.

00:07:44.661 --> 00:07:45.896
And more importantly,

00:07:45.929 --> 00:07:49.733
she consistently showed me
that she would never judge me if I failed.

00:07:52.803 --> 00:07:54.438
Eventually, I got the message.

00:07:54.471 --> 00:07:56.306
It took a while,

00:07:56.306 --> 00:07:59.476
but that unconditional love
that I received

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:02.312
allowed me to take the plunge,

00:08:02.312 --> 00:08:05.883
drop my guard, lower my defenses

00:08:05.916 --> 00:08:09.486
and identify what I was afraid of
and to share it with her.

00:08:11.488 --> 00:08:14.291
I think it's the hardest thing
I ever did my whole life.

00:08:14.324 --> 00:08:17.828
Definitely harder than anything
in the professional realm.

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:21.665
But there's nothing more worthwhile

00:08:21.698 --> 00:08:24.868
than taking our anxiety
and turning it into love.

00:08:26.603 --> 00:08:32.175
Losing control is utterly terrifying.

00:08:33.310 --> 00:08:34.745
It's terrifying.

00:08:34.778 --> 00:08:36.713
It's happened to everyone.

00:08:37.814 --> 00:08:40.484
But, but ...

00:08:42.085 --> 00:08:44.621
As long as you have a heads-up,

00:08:44.621 --> 00:08:48.792
as long as you expect it
and you're a willing participant,

00:08:48.825 --> 00:08:51.228
doesn't it feel good to let go?

00:08:54.464 --> 00:08:58.302
You don't need to be a thrill-seeker
to appreciate this.

00:08:58.335 --> 00:08:59.736
Adrenaline ...

00:09:00.737 --> 00:09:03.073
A shot of it comes with pure joy

00:09:03.106 --> 00:09:05.409
followed by this blissful tranquility,

00:09:05.442 --> 00:09:07.210
like, wow.

00:09:11.181 --> 00:09:12.549
And perhaps for that reason,

00:09:12.583 --> 00:09:18.288
even in this age of unprecedented,
incredible anxiety,

00:09:18.322 --> 00:09:19.990
action and adventure movies,

00:09:20.023 --> 00:09:23.160
they make up more than 50 percent
of box-office sales.

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:26.496
And the most profitable genre
of film is horror.

00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:27.698
(Laughter)

00:09:27.731 --> 00:09:28.999
It's funny.

00:09:29.032 --> 00:09:30.467
(Laughter)

00:09:31.301 --> 00:09:34.137
Now life isn't a movie,

00:09:34.171 --> 00:09:38.942
so it's very good to shape the world
in accordance with your vision

00:09:38.976 --> 00:09:40.177
on a daily basis.

00:09:40.210 --> 00:09:42.646
It's very important that we do that.

00:09:42.679 --> 00:09:44.781
But, once in a while ...

00:09:45.949 --> 00:09:49.286
It's a human need to take a seat

00:09:49.319 --> 00:09:52.689
and go for a ride
on the roller coaster of life,

00:09:52.723 --> 00:09:53.857
to let go.

00:09:53.890 --> 00:09:56.827
(Laughter)

00:09:58.195 --> 00:10:00.397
Doing so keeps your ego in check.

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:07.771
Some people view this surrender
in spiritual terms.

00:10:09.006 --> 00:10:10.574
The Serenity Prayer,

00:10:10.607 --> 00:10:14.978
very commonly used to cope with anxiety,

00:10:15.012 --> 00:10:16.580
and it famously states

00:10:16.613 --> 00:10:21.151
"God, grant me the serenity
to accept the things I cannot change."

00:10:22.753 --> 00:10:24.054
Now when you're ready --

00:10:24.087 --> 00:10:27.090
not before you're ready, please,
but when you're ready --

00:10:27.124 --> 00:10:30.894
affirming the limits of your control ...

00:10:31.762 --> 00:10:33.196
it brings inner peace.

00:10:34.931 --> 00:10:37.334
Anxiety is nothing to be ashamed of.

00:10:38.502 --> 00:10:40.037
We all have it.

00:10:41.805 --> 00:10:43.473
And it's not going away.

00:10:46.710 --> 00:10:51.615
Here are four steps that you can use

00:10:51.615 --> 00:10:54.117
to turn anxiety into your ally,
not your enemy.

00:10:54.151 --> 00:10:59.256
But please, if anxiety interferes
with your life, if it's clinical,

00:10:59.289 --> 00:11:01.091
don't just rely on this approach.

00:11:01.124 --> 00:11:03.026
Get the professional help you need.

00:11:03.026 --> 00:11:06.329
If we have an agreement on that,
then I'll tell you the four steps.

00:11:06.363 --> 00:11:08.832
(Laughter)

00:11:08.865 --> 00:11:11.668
OK. Step number one -- identify.

00:11:13.070 --> 00:11:16.073
Many times, when you feel anxious,
you squelch the sensations

00:11:16.106 --> 00:11:17.607
and push them out of your mind

00:11:17.641 --> 00:11:20.477
before you've even processed
what you're worried about.

00:11:20.510 --> 00:11:22.546
Stop.

00:11:22.579 --> 00:11:28.618
Take a minute and ask yourself,
"What am I truly afraid of?"

00:11:28.652 --> 00:11:31.088
Like what really is
at the bottom of my fear?

00:11:32.255 --> 00:11:34.324
If you don't know the answer, that's fine.

00:11:34.357 --> 00:11:37.160
Go for a walk and don't come back
until you have an answer.

00:11:37.160 --> 00:11:38.795
(Laughter)

00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:42.332
Step two -- share.

00:11:43.867 --> 00:11:46.336
Speak about your anxiety,

00:11:46.336 --> 00:11:49.306
with a friend, with a neighbor,
with a coworker,

00:11:49.339 --> 00:11:50.974
with a stranger.

00:11:52.342 --> 00:11:54.144
I'm serious.

00:11:55.946 --> 00:11:58.381
If you're not ready
for a conversation, that's fine.

00:11:58.415 --> 00:11:59.883
Text it.

00:11:59.916 --> 00:12:01.885
If it's more than a couple lines, sure.

00:12:01.918 --> 00:12:04.321
Email. Press send.

00:12:05.922 --> 00:12:09.392
Take the plunge. Be vulnerable.

00:12:10.861 --> 00:12:13.296
Step three -- embrace.

00:12:13.997 --> 00:12:15.398
When you feel anxious --

00:12:15.398 --> 00:12:18.368
not "if" -- you will.

00:12:18.401 --> 00:12:19.569
You will feel anxious.

00:12:19.569 --> 00:12:22.806
And when it happens, don't fight it.

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:25.642
Don't squelch it.

00:12:25.675 --> 00:12:28.779
Let it happen, let it ride, let it ride.

00:12:30.213 --> 00:12:33.116
In fact, do things
that make you uncomfortable.

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:35.452
Intentionally. Repeatedly.

00:12:35.485 --> 00:12:38.288
As long as they're safe.

00:12:38.288 --> 00:12:41.424
That's how we build emotional resilience.

00:12:42.692 --> 00:12:44.327
And finally, my favorite, four.

00:12:44.361 --> 00:12:46.229
Let go.

00:12:47.631 --> 00:12:49.266
Let go.

00:12:49.266 --> 00:12:52.002
Think back to step number one.

00:12:52.035 --> 00:12:53.436
What are you truly afraid of?

00:12:53.470 --> 00:12:57.174
And then, when you're ready, humbly admit,

00:12:57.207 --> 00:12:58.608
even for a moment,

00:12:58.642 --> 00:13:00.944
that you are not in full control
of that outcome.

00:13:03.046 --> 00:13:06.216
It's scary to even think about,
but it's not a bad thing.

00:13:06.249 --> 00:13:09.419
Firstly, sometimes challenges
are a blessing in disguise,

00:13:09.452 --> 00:13:13.223
but either way,

00:13:13.256 --> 00:13:18.061
enjoy not being responsible
for everything under the sun.

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:23.099
OK, should I try the four steps?

00:13:23.133 --> 00:13:24.901
Yeah, I'll give it a shot.

00:13:25.602 --> 00:13:26.736
Identify.

00:13:28.205 --> 00:13:32.776
The hardest part about this talk
was speaking about my anxiety in public.

00:13:34.277 --> 00:13:35.879
I was afraid you would judge me.

00:13:38.215 --> 00:13:39.583
It's really quiet in here.

00:13:39.616 --> 00:13:40.784
Did you judge me?

00:13:40.817 --> 00:13:42.752
(Laughter)

00:13:42.752 --> 00:13:44.454
OK. That made me really anxious.

00:13:44.487 --> 00:13:46.656
(Laughter)

00:13:46.690 --> 00:13:47.858
Share.

00:13:47.858 --> 00:13:49.693
OK, so I'm revealing this to you now

00:13:49.726 --> 00:13:51.962
because we've spent,
like, 10 minutes together,

00:13:51.995 --> 00:13:53.496
and I've grown to like you.

00:13:53.530 --> 00:13:56.032
So I want more of an emotional
connection here,

00:13:56.032 --> 00:13:57.734
and I hope it's mutual.

00:13:57.767 --> 00:13:58.768
(Laughter)

00:13:58.768 --> 00:13:59.936
OK, thanks.

00:13:59.970 --> 00:14:06.977
(Cheers and applause)

00:14:07.344 --> 00:14:08.478
(Exhales)

00:14:08.511 --> 00:14:09.546
(Laughter)

00:14:09.579 --> 00:14:10.814
Three -- embrace.

00:14:10.847 --> 00:14:14.150
Do you know what it's like
to stand on this red dot

00:14:14.150 --> 00:14:17.587
and to speak about,
like, all your issues in public?

00:14:17.587 --> 00:14:18.889
(Laughter)

00:14:18.922 --> 00:14:20.323
It's like diving off a cliff.

00:14:20.323 --> 00:14:23.260
Especially, remember that part
about my emotional kitchen?

00:14:23.293 --> 00:14:25.228
Like, that was really vulnerable for me.

00:14:25.228 --> 00:14:27.397
(Laughter)

00:14:27.430 --> 00:14:28.565
And let go.

00:14:28.598 --> 00:14:32.802
So I'm sending this message
about anxiety off into the universe.

00:14:32.836 --> 00:14:37.073
I hope that it will land on the hearts,
minds and souls of a broader audience.

00:14:37.107 --> 00:14:40.510
But really, there's nothing
I can do about that anymore.

00:14:40.543 --> 00:14:41.544
(Laughter)

00:14:41.578 --> 00:14:42.946
And that's OK.

00:14:43.313 --> 00:14:44.447
That's OK.

00:14:45.949 --> 00:14:47.217
So please join me.

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:48.418
What are the four steps?

00:14:48.451 --> 00:14:50.420
Let's say them together so we remember.

00:14:50.420 --> 00:14:54.991
(With the audience)
Identify, share, embrace, let go.

00:14:54.991 --> 00:14:56.192
Thank you very much.

00:14:56.226 --> 00:14:59.095
(Applause)

